NAME
       sync - write buffered data out

SYNOPSIS
       sync [-d] [-f] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
       Write buffered data out. With files, each one is
       synced; without, everything. The memory file system has
       nothing to write today, so this matters only once files
       are stored somewhere.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

